Once again I decided to plunge the depths of the Dungeons of Doom as my 
chaotic monk named heptapod.
I always play monk because it's supposedly really hard and anything worth 
doing is always difficult. I rarely pray, usually get lucky with food and 
end up with decent stats at the outset. This time around was frustrating 
since it took me until experience level 12 to get my first unicorn horn 
and I wasted a 1000+ turns hallucinating and abusing my wisdom. 
Thankfully my only companion was a peaceful red naga.
heptapod didn't have the best spells since I was unable to get him 
healing or sleep but he knew protection which I rarely cast unless I was 
going into a whole room full of trouble.
My equipment was fair, +3 gloves, +2 robe, +1 fireproof boots (that ended 
up being water-walking which made me feel stupid on the swamp level where 
I kept trying to sidestep the water when I really didn't have to) and a 
trusty orcish helm.
Dungeon level 19. My warning alerted me of a big room full of monsters 
with lots of 3s and 4s and moments later I got a message of "You hear the 
tones of courtly conversation." This was going to be fun. Unfortunately 
one of those 3s got loose and was coming straight towards me. It was a 
nurse! I stripped down and danced with her, lured her into a room and 
locked her inside for my hasty retreat when things became too hairy in 
the throne room.
Five dragons, lots of trolls (thank goodness I brought my tinning kit), a 
few giants and lots of orcs, goblins and hobgoblins. I beat my way in, 
hit a magic trap which blinded me and received a whupping. I read a 
scroll of teleportation (how can one do this while blinded?) and made it 
to safety. I danced around with my captive nurse to heal up and decided 
that I needed some fresh air.
Did I type #save??? No, I typed #quit instead of #save like a moron 
because I thought "quit, save then I'll come back later." AUGH. Why 
couldn't it have been a glorious death like "disintegrated by a black 
dragon" or "choked to death on a food ration"?
This was the farthest I had ever gotten and I'm sure that I would've 
gotten even farther and finally seen the darned castle that everyone 
talks about if only I thought before I typed.

